# Fluxo completo. Mesmo contrato dos templates Java e NestJS: troque @host para comparar.
# VS Code (REST Client) ou JetBrains HTTP Client. Rode na ordem.
@host = http://localhost:8080

### Cadastro (público)
# @name signup
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Ana", "email": "ana@example.com", "password": "secret123"}

### Login
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "ana@example.com", "password": "secret123"}

### Meu usuário
GET {{host}}/api/users/{{signup.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Renomear
PUT {{host}}/api/users/{{signup.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Ana Maria"}

### Boas-vindas (202; o log do consumer aparece logo depois)
POST {{host}}/api/users/{{signup.response.body.id}}/welcome
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Refresh (rotaciona: repetir esta mesma requisição dá 401)
# @name refresh
POST {{host}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.refreshToken}}"}

### Logout (revoga o refresh token novo; depois disso o refresh dá 401)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{"refreshToken": "{{refresh.response.body.refreshToken}}"}

### Login do admin de dev
# @name admin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "admin@example.com", "password": "admin12345"}

### Listar (só ADMIN)
GET {{host}}/api/users?page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Remover (soft delete; derruba as sessões)
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/{{signup.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}
